load-job-v1: the customer load job, the text Peeps gives a repository's
peeps.yml for load runs (CW).

Peeps' source of truth is src/lib/repo-backed/load-workflow.ts
(loadJobTemplate, loadJobSpec, the dispatch input lines and the guard).
Peeps' load-workflow.test.ts and the three templates' tests compare every
file here with what that module and the templates render.

The action copies this folder byte for byte and pins the same root hash: the
sha256 of MANIFEST without its first line, the status line, so marking the
corpus frozen does not change the hash. The copy of each refusal is outside
it, in ../load-job-v1-copy/refusal-copy.json: an edit there is not a change
of meaning.

Status: draft until the action's load release (A5). While draft, both
repositories change it together. Once frozen, a change of meaning is
load-job-v2.

Every file is rendered with the pins
  actionSha   0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567
  peepsOrigin https://dev.peepsai.com
and the golden templates with testRoot ".", defaultBranch "main", no config.

Files:
  peeps-load-job.yml        the peeps-load job, appended under jobs:
  dispatch-input-lines.yml  the two workflow_dispatch inputs it reads
  not-load-if.txt           the guard on the repository's ordinary job
  control-origins.json      the Peeps origins the action accepts for load
  refusal-codes.json        the action's refusal codes and their slot names
  golden/*.yml              each template rendered whole with the pins
